<title>USA: CPC says to take Q2 restructuring charge.</title>
<headline>CPC says to take Q2 restructuring charge.</headline>
<dateline>ENGLEWOOD CLIFFS, N.J. 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>CPC International Inc. and Subsidiaries</p>
<p>	    Consolidated Statements of Income</p>
<p>		 (All figures are in thousands</p>
<p>		   except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				  Three Months Ended March 31,</p>
<p>					     1997	     1996</p>
<p> Net sales			  $2,149,456     $2,099,421</p>
<p> Cost of sales		     1,210,298	1,206,370</p>
<p> Gross profit			  939,158	  893,051</p>
<p> Operating expenses		  706,086	  675,691</p>
<p>Operating income from</p>
<p>   continuing operations	   233,072	  217,360</p>
<p> Financing costs			37,398	   36,749</p>
<p>Income from continuing operations</p>
<p>   before income taxes	     195,674	  180,611</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes	 70,443	   66,826</p>
<p>					   125,231	  113,785</p>
<p> Minority stockholders' interest   7,774	    6,094</p>
<p>Income from continuing</p>
<p>  operations			   117,457	  107,691</p>
<p>Income (loss) from discontinued</p>
<p>operations, net of income taxes</p>
<p>   ($ (5))-1997; $9-1996)	     (8,558)	 14,735</p>
<p> Net income			     108,899	 122,426</p>
<p>Average common shares</p>
<p> outstanding			    143,504	 145,623</p>
<p>Earnings (loss) per common share</p>
<p>   Continuing operations		  .79	     .72</p>
<p>   Discontinued operations	    (.06)	     .10</p>
<p> Net earnings per common share	  .73	     .82</p>
<p>Cash dividends declared</p>
<p>   per common share			 .41	     .38</p>
<p>The company also said in conjunction with the spin-off of the corn refining operations, it will take a restructuring charge for the realignment of its packaged food operations as well as the reduction of corporate overhead costs.  The charge will be taken in the second quarter when costs associated with these activities have been determined.  CPC is currently reviewing its packaged food operations around the world to increase effectiveness and focus on core businesses.</p>
<p>This is an unaudited interim statement prepared by management and reflects all adjustments which are, in the opinion of management, necessary to a fair statement of results for the interim periods. Englewood Cliffs, NJ, April 14, 1997 James W. Ripley, Comptroller</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
